# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check text files out with LF
# everywhere. Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true gets
# CRLF, and two files here break in ways that are hard to read:
#
#   docker-entrypoint.sh  — `sh` treats the trailing \r as part of the last
#                           argument, so the container dies with an error
#                           naming a command that looks correct.
#   scripts/demo.sh       — same, and it is the first thing a reader runs.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs the entrypoint straight from the build context, so
# nothing downstream would fix it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF regardless of anything a contributor has set
# locally — the two above are executed, not just read.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never touched: mangling these corrupts them.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
